      "math_academy_id": "q-178162",
      "sequence_position": 17,
      "problem": "$$\n{{\\overset{P}{\\overset{⏞}{0\\le -1}}\\,\\overset{∨}{\\overset{⏞}{\\text{or}}}\\,\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{3\\,|\\,7}}}_{⏟}}_{P\\,∨\\,Q}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{14\\text{ is prime}}_{⏟}}_{R}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $P∨Q$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $R$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $(P∨Q)∨R$ is {{field-3}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is false, $Q$ is false, and $R$ is false. Therefore, $P∨Q$ is false, and the result is false:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(P∨Q)∨R & ≡\\overset{\\text{false}}{\\overset{⏞}{(\\text{false}∨\\text{false})}}∨\\text{false} \\\\  & ≡\\text{false}∨\\text{false} \\\\  & ≡\\text{false}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
